# Phase 1 C++ Adapter

This directory contains the Phase 1 C++ adapter for yescrypt.

`yescrypt_cpp.h` and `yescrypt_cpp.cpp` intentionally provide only a small,
type-safe C++ interface over the existing `yescrypt_hash` C entry point. The
algorithm remains in the existing C implementation until the Phase 2 port is
complete.

The adapter accepts exactly the 80-byte input and produces exactly the 32-byte
output used by `yescrypt_hash`. It does not change consensus behavior.

## Example

```cpp
#include <array>
#include <cstdint>
#include "crypto/yescrypt/yescrypt_cpp.h"

std::array<std::uint8_t, yescrypt::Hash::INPUT_SIZE> input{};
std::array<std::uint8_t, yescrypt::Hash::OUTPUT_SIZE> output{};
const auto result = yescrypt::Hash::Compute(input, output);
```

Phase 1 validation should compare `Hash::Compute` output with the existing
`yescrypt_hash` output for deterministic 80-byte test vectors. The C API remains
available for existing callers, including `CHashWriterYescrypt` in `src/hash.h`.
